<title>ZAIRE: Mobutu returns to Zaire after peace talks cancelled.</title>
<headline>Mobutu returns to Zaire after peace talks cancelled.</headline>
<dateline>KINSHASA 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zairean President Mobutu Sese Seko flew back to the capital Kinshasa on Thursday after an abortive bid to hold a second round of talks with rebel leader Laurent Kabila.</p>
<p>Airport sources said he flew in from Pointe Noire in neighbouring Congo where he spent the night after Kabila, reportedly raising new security concerns, declined to join the South African sponsored talks.</p>
</text>
